# loop-catch

The phone catches its own answer from the loop with its camera, on the public site's /ask/.

- [x] site/assets/js/catch.mjs: one catch per bottle id until the index names ours; others' frames let go after
- [x] site/assets/js/camera.mjs: the camera as a code reader (secure pages only; `can()` says first)
- [x] ask.js moved into the site (one script for the door's /ask/ and the public /ask/); "Catch it from the loop"
      where a camera may open; the LAN-only parts (set it down, ask the door) behind config `lan`
- [x] site/you/wizards/ask.md: the public /ask/ (pass layout, offline: true, unlisted)
- [x] test: a phone joining mid-loop, losing 30% of frames, keeps only its own answer from three; the built site's
      /ask/ on a secure page makes a signed bottle (intake: signed, wizard:model+ask)
- [ ] deploy the site when Autumn says (bin/deploy-site); the init bottle from qr.local
